==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The Metal Hippoe is the main issue, as it makes it unnecessarily difficult to hit Le'Solar. [[Moneko (Special Cat)|Miss MONEKO]] will probably be the only [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] Special Cat in your arsenal, but remember that [[Critical Hit]]s aren't the only way you can win; though if one owns [[Crazed Moneko (Special Cat)|Crazed Moneko]], [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million-Dollar Cat]] or [[Felix the Cat Duke Cat (Special Cat)|Felix the Cat Duke Cat]], this stage will be much easier with their guaranteed critical hit, though Crazed Moneko's short range and long foreswing is hard to work around, Million-Dollar Cat needs a minor boost to even be able to oneshot the Metal Hippoe, alongside the fact it's only obtainable during a certain part of the year and that Felix is a [[Tower of Saviors Collaboration Event|collab]] unit. At the 250% buff it appears with, Metal Hippoe takes 200 hits to get rid of; using rapid and/or [[:Category:Multi-Hit Cats|multi-hit]] attackers like [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Riceball Cat]] can speed up the process.

You may think [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]]'s first form may do better here, but his True Form is better here to kill the Star Pengs more quickly as not to waste time and lose to losing ground; his first form is too slow at killing the Star Pengs.

At the start, summon your critter once it is available, and spam meatshields throughout the entire battle to give yourself time before all Star Pengs come out. Summon [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Frog Ninja Cats]] or [[Dom Cat (Special Cat)|Dark Lazers]] for extra hits to quickly destroy any [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metals]], but not too many so you can save up quickly to summon Bahamut, who will be used later. You should stall until all Star Pengs are out and stacked up, then kill them with Awakened Bahamut once they're stacked up to where they can be killed much more easily, and finish off Le'Solar with not much hassle.

If you have extra slots available use any [[Cat Combo]] for Attack or Defense.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Chapter 2 changes things significantly by replacing Metal Hippoe with an UltraBaaBaa. While UltraBaaBaa can be taken out more quickly and consistently than Metal Hippoe, options for doing so are even fewer: you effectively have to use either [[Skirt Cat (Special Cat)|Loincloth Cat]], [[Li'l Gross Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Macho Legs]] or the [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast Cannon]] to shatter her [[Barrier]]. On the other hand, stalling UltraBaaBaa utilizing her Barrier allows units such as [[:Category:Mythic Cats|Mythic Cats]] to be stacked more easily and the [[Worker Cat]] to be leveled up. Note that you should stall UltraBaaBaa close to the enemy base, so that your legend units don't die while your loincloth cat is trying to catch up to the UltraBaaBaa that spawns on base hit. A similar strategy should be used as the one above, just with a Barrier Breaker instead of a critter.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
In Chapter 3, UltraBaaBaa is taken out of the stage and [[Metal Hippoe]] is back, but there are still only two Star Pengs and not three like in Chapter 1, making it easier than ever to just stall the enemies with meatshields until both Pengs have spawned, then lure them to the [[Cat Base]] and use [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] to take care of them. Metal Hippoe is so slow that by the time it makes it to the frontlines, both Star Pengs should be dead or about to die.

